/// Datasheet for the `physics` device — basic axis-aligned-rectangle (AABB) bodies in a float world.
///
/// Requirements only (components + a storage minimum): a `Body` (defined in physics.arche) is a centre
/// `pos` (the shared `vec` 2-vector), `half`-extents (a rectangle is centre ± half), a `vel`, and a `push`
/// accumulator the collision pass fills and `physics.shift` applies (two-phase resolve, so every body
/// reads the same pre-resolve positions — the boids `nvel`/`apply` split). The driver owns and sizes the
/// pool; `[4]Body` is a mild storage floor (the device works with any count).
vel(x, y)  :: float;
half(x, y) :: float;
push(x, y) :: float;

[4]Body;
